From 61db6b118895dfebd9408d334b8b56828c5e904c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:38:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] Round 1: Add the typed score-matrix API

Add Prepared::score_matrix and MatrixScore, which evaluate untraced
row-major parameter vectors without candidate or record JSON. Budget
parsing, limits, worker dispatch, deadlines, cancellation and failure
classification are shared with scores_json through one dispatch helper.
The Python extension gains a GIL-free score_matrix native method and
Prepared.score_matrix accepts lists of lists or 2-D NumPy arrays.
The benchmark gains a CRAFT_MATRIX API mode, performance_pair.py gains
--before-matrix/--after-matrix (metrics and detail normalized to null)
and optimize_performance.py gains --matrix.

Workload: serial (96 SIR candidates, one worker), lean scores_json
before, matrix after, 11 samples.
Before median: 14.611 ms. After median: 13.288 ms. Speedup: 1.10x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
